+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Infinite PSNR:** If MSE is 0, PSNR is infinite. Implementations must handle this by capping the value, using a small epsilon, or flagging it, as infinite values disrupt aggregation [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Alpha Channels:** Ground truth images often contain alpha channels (transparency), while NeRFs typically render RGB. A shared preprocessing step is compositing the ground truth RGBA image with a white background to ensure fair comparison with the rendered RGB image [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+*   **Shape Mismatch:** Rendered and ground truth images must have identical shapes. Mismatches should be skipped or handled via resizing/cropping [S2, unofficial].
 
